[size=5][b]Falkos Lichtspiel[/b][/size]
Hardware raytracing for Skyrim SE/AE, built on [b]Community Shaders 1.9[/b] and [b]Creation Engine Raytracing[/b].

Falkos Lichtspiel is a complete replacement for Community Shaders: all Community Shaders 1.9 features plus a hardware-raytracing backend with several modes, from a light hybrid mode to full raytraced global illumination.

[color=#ffcc00][b]Beta.[/b] Tested by the author on one PC (RTX 5080). Other GPUs are untested. Please report bugs on GitHub (link below), not to the Community Shaders or CER developers.[/color]

[size=4][b]Raytracing modes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]RT AO[/b] – raytraced ambient occlusion only. Low cost.
[*][b]RT Lights[/b] – all local lights (torches, candles, fires, magic, lamps) raytraced, with real shadows from the strongest lights. Medium cost.
[*][b]RT Lights + AO[/b] – both together.
[*][b]Global Illumination[/b] – raytraced indirect diffuse and specular light. High cost.
[*][b]Path Tracing[/b] – experimental. Very high cost.
[/list]
In the hybrid modes the sun, sky light and reflections stay raster. With raytracing disabled at boot, the mod costs nothing extra.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Skyrim SE 1.5.97 or AE 1.6.x (not VR)
[*]SKSE64
[*]Address Library for SKSE Plugins
[*]SSE Engine Fixes (required for raytracing)
[*]Crash Logger SSE AE VR (required for raytracing)
[*]Windows 10/11, a GPU with hardware raytracing (DXR 1.1) for the RT modes. DLSS Ray Reconstruction is NVIDIA RTX only.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Disable or remove Community Shaders[/b] and its feature add-ons. Falkos Lichtspiel uses the same file names and replaces them. Do not install both.
[*]Install the main file with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex.
[*]In game, open the menu with [b]End[/b] → Raytracing → Mode.
[/list]
Optional file [i]PDBs[/i]: debug symbols for readable Crash Logger logs.

[size=4][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]RT Lights: only the 4 strongest lights per pixel cast shadows; weaker lights are unshadowed.
[*]Transparent objects, particles and hair keep raster lighting in the RT Lights modes.
[*]After a loading screen, distant objects can join the raytraced lighting a moment later (intended, avoids stutter).
[*]AMD and Intel GPUs are untested.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Bug reports[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/falkoniumzzz-jpg/SkyrimRTLab/issues]GitHub issues[/url] – please attach CommunityShaders.log, CreationEngineRaytracing.log (Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE) and the Crash Logger log if the game crashed.

